Requirements:
- Exactly one murderer, who must be one of the suspects (never the victim).
- The murderer must be an actor in a timeline event at {{ setting.get('murder_location', 'the crime scene') }}
  at the time of death.
- No person may be in two different places at the same time. Watchers and
  actors both count as present.
- Every suspect has at least one secret. At least one innocent suspect has a
  secret that makes them look suspicious for an unrelated reason (mark it
  `is_red_herring: true`).
- 5 to 8 clues. At least two non-red-herring clues have `points_to` set to the
  murderer.
- **Fair play — guilt must be genuinely hard to deduce:**
  - Clues are circumstantial, not conclusive. Do NOT name the culprit outright
    in a clue description, and avoid unique identifying details (monograms,
    initials, handwriting) that point at exactly one suspect.
  - At least two clues must be red herrings (`is_red_herring: true`), and they
    must point at **two different innocents** (set `points_to`), so the culprit
    is not the only person a clue implicates.
  - At least three different suspects should be implicated by some clue
    (red-herring or not), and several suspects should have both motive and
    opportunity.
- Every id you reference (locations, actors, witnesses, `points_to`, victim,
  murderer, crime_location) must exist elsewhere in the same JSON.

